      "content": "Undergoing any unauthorized increase in medication dosage carries risks, such as changes in blood pressure, potassium levels, or even cardiac risk. Though self-titration is not common, healthcare providers also advise against it due to the potential for harm and complications. Your doctor's office can usually prioritize an appointment, even if it's not an emergency, due to your symptom. In the meantime, for your well-being, try to stand up slowly from sitting or lying positions, keep hydrated, and continue monitoring your blood pressure if you have a way to do so at home. However, please seek an appointment with your doctor as soon as possible to address your dizziness and any concerns with your lisinopril treatment.",
